quiet.md #26: replace_root updates the window handle's root type

Window::replace_root swapped the root view but left the handle (and the copy
in App::window_handles) recording the old root type, so downcast::<New>()
kept failing. First launch replaces the onboarding view with the workspace in
the same window, and code that looks for the workspace window could not find
it.

diff --git a/crates/gpui/src/window.rs b/crates/gpui/src/window.rs
index 7331f559c749a73d8b6451127519c379f27c509d..2b654aae7caee7ba1606d434f1ab0f0a07d4cb63 100644
--- a/crates/gpui/src/window.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui/src/window.rs
@@ -2670,6 +2670,10 @@ impl Window {
     {
         let view = cx.new(|cx| build_view(self, cx));
         self.root = Some(view.clone().into());
+        // quiet.md: the window's handle says what its root is: `downcast` to
+        // the new type must find it.
+        self.handle.state_type = TypeId::of::<E>();
+        cx.window_handles.insert(self.handle.id, self.handle);
         self.refresh();
         view
     }
